<Base title="Research" description="BTVSL, a sentence-level dataset for Bangla Sign Language translation, published at IEEE FG 2024." jsonLd={[article]}>
  <header class="article-head">
    <h1>Research</h1>
    <p class="lede">My research so far is on Bangla Sign Language. It started as my undergraduate thesis at BUET, supervised by Dr. Muhammad Abdullah Adnan.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="pubs-h">
    <h2 id="pubs-h">Publication</h2>
    <article class="paper prose">
      <h3>
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/FG59268.2024.10581873">BTVSL: A Novel Sentence-Level Annotated Dataset for Bangla Sign Language Translation</a>
      </h3>
      <p class="paper-authors"><strong>Iftekhar E Mahbub Zeeon</strong>, Mir Mahathir Mohammad, Muhammad Abdullah Adnan</p>
      <p class="paper-venue">
        2024 IEEE 18th International Conference on Automatic Face and Gesture Recognition (FG), Istanbul, May 2024, pages 1–10.
      </p>
      <ul class="project-links">
        <li><a href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10581873">IEEE Xplore</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/FG59268.2024.10581873">DOI</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/6105c8371868e79251b832e3ff2ca8c5e62d4de2">Semantic Scholar</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h4>What the paper is about</h4>
      <p>
        Sign language is a vital way to communicate for people with hearing impairments, and Bangla Sign Language is
        widely used in the Bangla-speaking community. Most earlier research could only recognise single signs or
        words, in controlled settings with small datasets. Translating whole signed sentences into Bangla
        text was hardly studied, because no large dataset existed for it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We built BTVSL from the BTV news programme "Desh o Jonopoder Khobor", where professional interpreters sign
        the news. The dataset holds 60 hours of signed news, matched sentence by sentence with Bangla text. When we
        published it, it was the largest sentence-level dataset for Bangla Sign Language translation.
      </p>
      <p>
        We trained four translation models on BTVSL. They reached an average BLEU score of 20.42. BLEU is a standard
        score that compares a machine translation with a human one.
      </p>
      <p class="quiet">Later Bangla sign language datasets cite BTVSL as earlier work. Semantic Scholar lists 4 citations as of November 2026.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
